                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Probably Thomas Hookham, bookseller, publisher, etc., who published the first edition of <title>Queen Mab</title>, 
    then trading at T Hookham and E.T. Hookham of 15 Old Bond Street.  
    Other incarnations of the publishing firm include:  	 Hookham and Carpenter (1791-9); Hookham and Ebers (1803-8); T and E Hookham (1809-13); T Hookham and Sons (1811-5); 
    Hookham and Sons (1817-20). He was the brother of <persName key="HOO02">E Hookham</persName>.</p>
                    </note>
